0.12 0.24 0.42 rg
BT /F2 8 Tf 50 812 Td (SMARTNOTE AI  |  PROJECT EVALUATION GUIDE) Tj ET
0.75 0.80 0.87 RG 0.7 w 50 802 m 545 802 l S
0.25 0.30 0.38 rg
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 34 Td (Simple-language study guide) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 500 34 Td (Page 6 of 7) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 775 Tm (A fallback is a simpler local method used if a cloud AI service is unavailable. This project) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 763 Tm (  has local fallbacks for notes, topics, and practice, but not for chat.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 749 Tm (10. What is the purpose of chunk overlap?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 732 Tm (It repeats a small part of text between neighboring chunks so a sentence or idea near a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 720 Tm (  boundary is less likely to lose context.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 706 Tm (11. Where is the API key stored?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 689 Tm (In a local .env file or through API settings. The file is ignored by Git and the key should) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 677 Tm (  never be committed or shared.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 663 Tm (12. Why might chat return an error even if a key exists?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 646 Tm (The model might not be available to the account, the key may be invalid, the network may fail,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 634 Tm (  or free-tier quota/rate limits may be reached.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 620 Tm (13. What happens after a server restart?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 603 Tm (The startup handler deletes saved uploaded PDFs and document JSON. The app currently does not) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 591 Tm (  preserve uploaded documents across restarts.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 577 Tm (14. How is chat history sent?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 560 Tm (The browser stores recent messages in memory and sends a limited number with the next) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 548 Tm (  question. The server adds them to the Gemini prompt.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 534 Tm (15. What is one improvement you would make?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 517 Tm (I would add an optional document-grounded chat mode that retrieves relevant chunks, includes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 505 Tm (  them in the Gemini prompt, and cites their pages. I would also add OCR for scanned PDFs and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 493 Tm (  persistent storage.) Tj ET
BT /F2 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 475 Tm (SHORT PRESENTATION SCRIPT) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 450 Tm (Good morning. My project is SmartNote AI, a study assistant for lecture PDFs. The user uploads) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 438 Tm (  a PDF through the web interface. The FastAPI backend receives it, and PyMuPDF extracts text) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 426 Tm (  page by page. The processor also records page information and creates text chunks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 409 Tm (The AI service uses Gemini to generate structured notes, important topics, and practice) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 397 Tm (  questions. If those Gemini operations fail, the application has local heuristic fallbacks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 385 Tm (  The chat feature is different: it sends the question and recent conversation directly to) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 373 Tm (  Gemini, so it can answer general questions but is not currently grounded in the uploaded) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 361 Tm (  PDF.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 344 Tm (The frontend is built with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. It calls backend routes and displays the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 332 Tm (  returned material. The project also has a TF-IDF and cosine-similarity retrieval component,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 320 Tm (  automated tests, and Markdown or printable HTML exports. Important limitations are that) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 308 Tm (  scanned PDFs need OCR, documents are cleared on server startup, and live AI features depend) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 296 Tm (  on model access and quota.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 279 Tm (That is the complete flow: upload, extract, generate, and display.) Tj ET
BT /F2 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 258 Tm (GLOSSARY) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 233 Tm (- API: a defined way for two software parts to communicate.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 219 Tm (- Backend: the server-side code that handles data and application logic.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 205 Tm (- Frontend: the part of the application the user sees and interacts with.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 191 Tm (- Endpoint: a specific API URL for one operation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 177 Tm (- JSON: a text format for structured data exchanged between the browser and server.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 163 Tm (- Chunk: a smaller piece of a longer document.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 149 Tm (- Embedding/vector: a list of numbers representing text for comparison.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 135 Tm (- TF-IDF: a method that scores words by their importance in a document.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 121 Tm (- Cosine similarity: a way to compare how similar two vectors are.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 107 Tm (- RAG: retrieval first, then generation using the retrieved information.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 93 Tm (- Heuristic: a practical rule-based approximation, not a full language model.) Tj ET
endstream
